# Tailscale devices

## Gate

Use when the user asks which devices are on the tailnet, online status,
tags, IPs, advertised routes, exit nodes, or netmap shape. Skip ACL-policy
authoring (use `tailscale-acls`) unless a device tag must be resolved.

## Transport

No Tailscale MCP was discovered for this harness. Prefer:

1. Local `tailscale` CLI when the agent host is on the tailnet.
2. Else Tailscale Admin API (`api.tailscale.com`) with a resolved tailnet
   id and API access token from the operator’s secret store / env —
   never hardcode hosts or paste tokens into chat.

If a Tailscale MCP appears later, use its list/describe tools when ready
— **do not invent MCP tool names**.

## Resolve ids

Never invent device id, hostname, MagicDNS name, or Tailscale IP. Resolve
from the user, a prior list this turn, or:

| Need | CLI / API |
| --- | --- |
| Local status | `tailscale status` · `tailscale status --json` |
| Self IPs | `tailscale ip -4` · `tailscale ip -6` |
| Netcheck | `tailscale netcheck` |
| Ping peer | `tailscale ping HOSTNAME` (connectivity probe only) |
| Tailnet devices | `GET /api/v2/tailnet/{tailnet}/devices` |
| One device | `GET /api/v2/device/{deviceId}` |

Resolve `{tailnet}` from operator config / env (for example
`TAILSCALE_TAILNET`) — often an org domain or tailnet name — never invent
it.

If several devices match a short name, list candidates (hostname + IP +
online) and ask once.

## Receipt shape

Report: **hostname**, **Tailscale IP(s)**, **online/offline**, **tags**,
**OS**, advertised/exit routes when relevant. Never paste auth keys, API
tokens, or OAuth client secrets.

## Routes / exit nodes (read)

| Need | Source |
| --- | --- |
| Advertised routes | device `AllowedIPs` / `PrimaryRoutes` from status JSON or API |
| Exit node candidates | devices advertising `0.0.0.0/0` / `::/0` or exit-node flag |
| Local exit use | `tailscale status` exit-node field |

Advertising new subnet/exit routes is a mutate → `tailscale-safety` plus
an explicit verb naming the device and prefixes.

## Mutate (gated)

| Action | Shape |
| --- | --- |
| Delete / expire device | Admin API `DELETE /api/v2/device/{deviceId}` |
| Enable/disable key expiry | API device update fields the operator named |
| Approve routes | API route approval when the tailnet requires it |

All need an **explicit verb this turn naming the device**. Prefer disable
/ expire over delete when the user did not say delete.

## Defaults

1. Read-only status/list is the default.
2. Cap large device lists; filter by tag or online state when possible.
3. Headscale / plain WireGuard meshes are out of scope unless the user
   named Tailscale.
4. After an authorized mutate, re-list/status and report the new state.

## Refuse

- Inventing device ids, tags, or route prefixes.
- Pasting auth keys or API tokens into chat.
- Claiming a device exists without status/list this turn.
